SCRIPT:NEWRULEHINT
"Return to the notice board to read more rules."
END

SCRIPT:NEWRULE01
"THE NEW RULES \n \n As spoken by Sharkey, Lord of the Shire \n Abbreviated for the Purpose of Signage and thus Non-Exhaustive \n For a full Charter, set an appointment with The Chief."
END

SCRIPT:NEWRULE02
"Rule Number One \n \n It is hereby Ordered that no Hobbit shall gather, keep, or consume ale, beer, cider, or other strong drink save by Licence duly granted by the Chief's Men, and only in such quantity as they shall deem fit."
END

SCRIPT:NEWRULE03
"Rule Number Two \n \n  No tree shall be felled, pruned, climbed, or otherwise meddled with except by express Written Permission; provided always that the Chief's Men may cut whatsoever trees they require, without notice or appeal."
END

SCRIPT:NEWRULE04
"Rule Number Three\n \n Every Hobbit between the ages of fifteen and one hundred shall present himself for Labour when called upon, and any refusal, delay, or complaint shall be deemed wilful Idleness and punished accordingly."
END

SCRIPT:NEWRULE05
"... The list goes on."
END

SCRIPT:NEWRULE06
"... The first few pages appear torn off. Only the last few remain:"
END

SCRIPT:NEWRULE07
"Rule Number Seventeen \n \n No gathering exceeding three persons shall be held in any inn, lane, field, or dwelling after sunset without Leave first obtained from the Shiriffs. Conversation touching upon former customs, absent persons, or matters of governance shall be especially discouraged."
END

SCRIPT:NEWRULE08
"Rule Number Eighteen \n \n Any speech tending to bring the Chief, his Rules, his Men, or the New Order into Ridicule, Contempt, or Disrepute shall be accounted Mischief of a Serious Nature, whether spoken plainly, hinted broadly, sung, muttered, or overheard."
END

SCRIPT:NEWRULE09
"Rule Number Nineteen \n \n No weapons of any kind shall be kept or carried by Hobbits without special permission, and any such items found shall be seized."
END

SCRIPT:NEWRULE10
"Rule Number Twenty \n \n All former customs and traditions shall give way to these Rules, which shall take precedence in all matters, and any uncertainty shall be resolved in favour of the Chief and his authority."
END

